{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/2","id":4893575933,"node_id":"PR_kwDON1sLX88AAAABI64K_Q","html_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/2","diff_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/2.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/2.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/2","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/2/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/2/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/2/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/statuses/1dbaadbb2d83af7b6169e1bccf445b26107b6237","number":2,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Personal biography & CV website with infographics, case study and Pages deploy fix","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #1\n\n## Summary\n\nThis builds konard.github.io as a public biography and CV with a dark, futuristic look. It uses infographics instead of plain lists.\n\nAll facts come from public sources collected in this PR, and every number is generated from committed data snapshots. The site makes no runtime API calls.\n\nThe full analysis is in [`docs/case-studies/issue-1/README.md`](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-1-c88f52c0d8c8/docs/case-studies/issue-1/README.md). It covers:\n- every requirement from the issue;\n- the options considered and the solution chosen for each;\n- a comparison with existing libraries (Recharts, D3, visx, Nivo, ECharts, Chart.js, react-chrono, github-readme-stats, gitprofile, JSON Resume, react-three-fiber, …);\n- the CI root causes;\n- the data conflicts and the choices made for them.\n\n## Sections and infographics\n\n| Requirement | Section | Visualization |\n|---|---|---|\n| Biography | Hero | Avatar with a rotating neon ring, headline, bio, \"open to collaboration & hire\" badge, Print / PDF CV button |\n| Overview | Stat tiles | 132K contributions, 1,460 repositories, gists, ~305 packages, ~2.5M lifetime downloads, stars, followers, years coding |\n| Companies | 01 Companies & ventures | Gantt career chart (2006–2026). Employment is solid and open-source ventures are hatched. Below it are position cards with role, summary and stack |\n| Projects | 02 Open-source ecosystem, 05 Featured projects | Orbit map of the personal account and 4 organizations (area = repositories). Project cards filterable by language, with star bars |\n| Languages | 03 Contributions & languages | Contributions per year (log/linear toggle, data table). Repositories by primary language (top 10 + Other) |\n| Technologies | 04 Technologies | Matrix of 8 groups: languages, formats, databases, frameworks, .NET, DevOps, tools, domains |\n| Other CV sections | 06 Published packages, 07 Community, writing & education, 08 Method | npm, crates.io and NuGet panels with top-package bars. Stack Overflow tag bars. Habr articles and talks. Education and highlights. The owner's problem-solving algorithm |\n| Social media | 09 Contacts & social media | 15 profiles: GitHub, Telegram, X, LinkedIn, YouTube, Habr, Habr Career, VK, Discord, Stack Overflow, CodersRank, npm, crates.io, NuGet, email |\n\nCharts are hand-written SVG/CSS; the app is 72.6 KB gzipped JS. They use one categorical palette validated for color-vision deficiency on the dark surface, and hatching as a second encoding. Tooltips work on hover and on keyboard focus. The layout is responsive, there is a print stylesheet, and `prefers-reduced-motion` is respected.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nDesktop (1440×900):\n\n![Hero](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-1-c88f52c0d8c8/docs/case-studies/issue-1/screenshots/desktop-hero.png?raw=true)\n\n![Career timeline](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-1-c88f52c0d8c8/docs/case-studies/issue-1/screenshots/section-experience.png?raw=true)\n\n![Ecosystem](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-1-c88f52c0d8c8/docs/case-studies/issue-1/screenshots/section-ecosystem.png?raw=true)\n\n![Contributions & languages](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-1-c88f52c0d8c8/docs/case-studies/issue-1/screenshots/section-activity.png?raw=true)\n\n![Technologies](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-1-c88f52c0d8c8/docs/case-studies/issue-1/screenshots/section-skills.png?raw=true)\n\n![Projects](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-1-c88f52c0d8c8/docs/case-studies/issue-1/screenshots/section-projects.png?raw=true)\n\n![Packages](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-1-c88f52c0d8c8/docs/case-studies/issue-1/screenshots/section-packages.png?raw=true)\n\n![Community](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-1-c88f52c0d8c8/docs/case-studies/issue-1/screenshots/section-community.png?raw=true)\n\n![Contacts](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-1-c88f52c0d8c8/docs/case-studies/issue-1/screenshots/section-contacts.png?raw=true)\n\nMobile (390×844):\n\n<img src=\"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-1-c88f52c0d8c8/docs/case-studies/issue-1/screenshots/mobile-hero.png?raw=true\" width=\"300\"> <img src=\"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-1-c88f52c0d8c8/docs/case-studies/issue-1/screenshots/mobile-timeline.png?raw=true\" width=\"300\">\n\n[Full-page screenshot](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-1-c88f52c0d8c8/docs/case-studies/issue-1/screenshots/desktop-full.png?raw=true)\n\n## CI / deploy fix\n\nNothing had ever been deployed: the Pages API reported `errored` for `main:/docs`. The original workflow had four defects:\n\n1. **Invalid YAML.** The step name `Deploy: Copy build…` contains an unquoted `: `. This failed run [38958801553](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/actions/runs/38958801553).\n2. **Nonexistent dependency.** The `@testing-library/react@^19` override does not exist (the latest version is 16.3.3).\n3. **Broken build.** `src/index.js` imported `reportWebVitals`, but `web-vitals` was never installed.\n4. **The deploy would delete docs.** `rm -rf docs` would have deleted `docs/case-studies`. It also used Node 14 and `actions/*@v3`.\n\nThe rewritten workflow:\n- runs tests and a build on pull requests and on `main`;\n- on `main` only, copies the build into `docs/` while keeping `docs/case-studies`;\n- uses Node 20 and `actions/*@v4`.\n\n## Data pipeline\n\n- **Collect:** `experiments/collect-github-data.sh` and `experiments/collect-contributions.sh` (via `gh api`) write snapshots to `docs/case-studies/issue-1/data/`, alongside npm, crates.io, NuGet and Stack Exchange API snapshots and `web-research.md` (online research with sources and confidence levels).\n- **Generate:** `npm run build:data` (`scripts/build-data.js`) writes `src/data/github.json`.\n- **Curate:** career, education, skills, publications and contacts are in `src/data/profile.js`.\n\n## Tests\n\n`npm run test:ci`: 28 tests in 4 suites.\n\n| Suite | What it checks |\n|---|---|\n| `src/App.test.js` | All sections render, nav anchors resolve, the timeline bar has an accessible label, contact links are safe, the log/linear toggle works, tooltips appear on focus, the language filter works |\n| `src/components/components.test.js` | Formatting, stat tiles, top-N with Other, project merging, timeline dates, contribution scale |\n| `src/data/data.test.js` | Experience dates are valid and ordered, featured projects exist, links are https or mailto, `github.json` matches `build-data.js` output, the noise filter works |\n| `src/workflow.test.js` | Every workflow is valid YAML, and the deploy keeps `docs/case-studies` |\n\n## Assumptions (details in the case study, section 8)\n\n- **Location:** \"Planet Earth · remote\". Sources disagree: Moscow, Goa, Planet Earth.\n- **Dates where sources disagree:** Deep.Foundation is shown from Jul 2020 and Abracar ends Aug 2022; Link.Assistant starts May 2025, from its earliest repository.\n- **Counts:** downloads count lifetime totals only (crates.io + NuGet); npm is shown per month. Repository charts use the 672 original repositories; forks and auto-generated log repositories are excluded.\n- **Not found online:** conference talks and peer-reviewed papers. LinkedIn and VK block automated fetches.\n\nThese are easy to adjust in `src/data/profile.js`.\n\nAfter merge, the workflow deploys the build to `docs/` on `main`, and GitHub Pages serves it from there.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-16T19:58:25Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T09:29:11Z","closed_at":"2026-10-17T09:29:11Z","merged_at":"2026-10-17T09:29:11Z","merge_commit_sha":"3d4aa8dfe5455358d3f7ba30a9557882ba3480a4","assignee":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_ur